{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D151-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"10b765a2fbbace5cd127afb859b8d8330598620c005cdfcf35c2eb271c4c5fc7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 recruits help choosing a destination, but A3 asks for support without making migration a useful explanation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 counters B2 with a packed chimney; A5 answers B4 but adds an unsupported watering hole.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 disputes migration and B4 asks where; neither gives B a practical stake.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 supplies a destination preference without increasing A1's commitment or consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a migrating house, but no immediate household problem explains the request.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's packed chimney is economical, while A5's watering hole adds animal imagery rather than useful logic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 54\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The house is migrating south. Help me redirect it before we lose the driveway.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The surveyor says subsidence. He's bringing concrete.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Concrete traps it halfway across the road. Tell him we're planning a route.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"His truck's blocking the road already.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Perfect. Ask him to lead slowly toward the empty plot. It needs a guide.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D151 recruits B to use an impossible explanation because it offers a workable account of what to do next.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D155 requests one premise-dependent choice; D151 seeks shared use of an explanatory framework.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 asks B to support the house's journey; revised A3 and A5 make migration govern the surveyor's concrete and truck.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a recruits a resistant homeowner through logistics; alternative b recruits a colleague through the kettle's supposed workplace grievance.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced decorative migration with a new driveway-and-surveyor situation. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 makes migration useful), logic 5 (A3 uses concrete; A5 uses B4's truck), relationship 4 (B2 brings a credible remedy), heightening 4 (A5 recruits the surveyor as guide), specificity 4 (A1 supplies the driveway problem), brevityWit 4 (A5 earns its guide idea): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The house following a guide remains a comic assumption; actors must sincerely treat it as the available solution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D151-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"af1c63649ea206f3fdbdb5b4e1dbc2b188c6759710fa97caac7a1bd2015d4b94\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 invites consultation with the kettle, but A5 explicitly labels the impossible instead of demonstrating its usefulness.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 makes B2's boil into an agenda; A5 acknowledges B4's proposed water.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 supply literal kettle functions without a separate need or meaningful cost.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 announces collaboration rather than developing B4's helpful water proposal.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a kettle but no occasion or practical reason to answer its complaints.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'collaborating with the impossible' explains the exercise instead of remaining natural character speech.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 56\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The office kettle's on strike. Help me negotiate before the clients arrive.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've filled it twice. It still won't boil.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then water isn't its grievance. Tell it we'll stop leaving it alone after meetings.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can take it into the meeting.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. Give it my chair. A seat at the table should get us tea.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D151 makes A enlist B in treating a bizarre explanation as a useful basis for joint problem-solving.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D158 redirects questions toward tasks without needing B to adopt an explanation; D151 actively recruits that adoption.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 interprets boiling as an agenda; revised A3 interprets failed refilling as evidence of a grievance and A5 proposes representation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The house alternative converts an outside expert into a guide; this alternative accepts B's help and sacrifices A's own chair.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a new office-client deadline and replaced the explanatory ending. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 advances the strike explanation), logic 5 (A3 uses failed filling; A5 uses B4's meeting offer), relationship 4 (B2 has already tried helping), heightening 4 (A5 yields A's chair), specificity 4 (A1 establishes office visitors), brevityWit 4 (A5's seat earns its double meaning): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The office-strike metaphor is familiar; the personal chair concession carries most of the final turn's freshness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D152-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"497fd4580c9e569126ed70f2a576e587e77e4d73a6f15b1c4ecfe787f646c1ca\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 delegates catching tomorrow, but neither A1 nor A5 supplies a practical way to distinguish tomorrow's water.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's refusal; A5 answers B4's measurement question with another undefined metaphor.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 resists doing the test and B4 reasonably asks what would count as evidence.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves to tasting but does not make the experiment more actionable or consequential.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 provides a cup without a source of water or a playable experimental setting.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's recorder excuse is concise; A5's 'ahead of schedule' obscures the requested action.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 55\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"This tap runs tomorrow's water. Fill that ice tray; we'll see whether it freezes before we chill it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why can't you fill it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm timing. Your finger's already on the tap.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll fill one cube. We need the rest for dinner.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One's enough. Leave it on the counter so the freezer can't take credit.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D152 gets B to perform the first concrete experiment that could substantiate a bizarre claim.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D155 asks for conduct conditional on a premise; D152 seeks an observable result that could establish the premise.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original B4 asks what would count as tomorrow's water; revised A1 supplies premature freezing as the test and A5 excludes the freezer.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a bargains with a household partner over dinner supplies; alternative b seeks a cautious crossing test from someone with equipment.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a new kitchen experiment with a visible criterion. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 delegates a test), logic 5 (A3 answers refusal; A5 accepts B4's one-cube limit), relationship 4 (B4 protects dinner supplies), heightening 4 (A5 specifies a control), specificity 4 (A1 identifies tap and tray), brevityWit 4 (A5's credit follows the experiment): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The freezing prediction is A's bizarre hypothesis, not an ordinary implication of water arriving from tomorrow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D152-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"1cc9f302aaa9e6fa01f0488560efc1b83e3f5faed7b08fd312e8558fcfed754d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks B to probe an invisible bridge; A5 persists after a negative result, slightly shifting toward unfalsifiable belief.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's umbrella question and A5 requests another probe because B4 reports no contact.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 questions use of their property, but A3 substitutes a confidence insult for a persuasive answer.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 requests another plank test without materially increasing commitment or refining the test.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 clearly establishes a crossing, an umbrella and A's desire to test before stepping.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's confidence line is compact but weakly motivated by B2's equipment question.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"There's an invisible bridge across this ditch. Tap for it with your umbrella before I cross.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Use your walking stick.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yours extends. You can test it without leaving the bank.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll extend it, but you're holding my belt.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Gladly. Reach until it touches something, then tell me whether it's above the water.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D152 makes A recruit B for an initial practical probe of an extraordinary claim.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic risk avoidance merely sends B first; D152 asks B to gather evidence that could verify the claim.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 requests an umbrella probe rather than B crossing; revised A5 distinguishes a possible bridge surface from water.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This version makes delegated testing a reciprocal safety bargain; alternative a uses domestic resource limits and a timing experiment.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the bridge and umbrella, specified a ditch, and replaced the insult with practical persuasion. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 requests a probe), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's substitute; A5 accepts B4's belt condition), relationship 4 (B4 requires support), heightening 4 (A5 commits A and sharpens the observation), specificity 4 (A1 locates the crossing), brevityWit 4 (A3 makes the umbrella choice meaningful): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"This is a clear playable bargain with modest wit; the physical situation requires imaginary rather than actual hazardous staging.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D153-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"c61105cfd257cd919a2c6dabe91eac6a241e264489bb17544132194b9d87d50c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands the drawing's date and A3 contrasts A's prediction with B's earlier disbelief.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's present visibility with prior detail; A5 turns B4's acknowledgment into a request for public credit.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 minimizes A's distinction and B4 offers limited praise, prompting A to demand a wider audience.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands B4's private 'Well done' to the people benefiting from the predicted staircase.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a floating staircase and dated drawing; A3's handrail gives the prior claim concrete detail.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'using my prediction to get upstairs' economically turns a prediction into a claimed public service.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I drew that floating staircase last week. Mention the date.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We can all see it now.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I drew the handrail while you called it nonsense.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Well done.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Loud enough for the people using my prediction to get upstairs.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D153 makes A obtain acknowledgment of having understood or accepted the impossible before everyone else.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary praise-seeking seeks admiration for an achievement; this card specifically demands recognition of earlier belief or knowledge.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1's 'last week' and A3's 'while you called it nonsense' establish temporal priority rather than merely claiming ownership.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a demands public recognition of a documented prediction; alternative b bargains for recognition of sustained private belief while being asked to keep quiet.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after rereading: A3 answers B2's dismissal, and B4's minimal acknowledgment causes A5 to demand audibility to beneficiaries. The original scores and 90 total remain appropriate; no improvement is invented.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 offers little resistance, and A5's ownership wording could briefly suggest invention rather than prediction; A1 and A3 preserve the distinction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D153-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a589945aa656baf0f8a45943ce47bb52c056593eee4090bc6bacf9b0ae447563\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims early belief and A3 requests acknowledgment, but A5 settles into defending long support rather than securing credit.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 bargains around B2's silence request; A5 reinterprets B4's criticism as familiarity.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 advocate the cupboard's desire for quiet, giving A a credible obstacle.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds years of support but drops A3's concrete request that B acknowledge it.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and B2 establish a newly speaking cupboard with an immediate wish for silence.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 economically converts 'talk too much' into evidence of a long relationship.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I believed this cupboard could speak when you wanted it scrapped. Say I was first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's asking for silence.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Whisper it. Then we can both respect its wishes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It says whispering counts.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Write it, then. 'You believed before any of us.' I'll put it beside its first words.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D153 drives A to secure explicit recognition of having accepted the impossible earlier than others.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Defending one's loyalty can resemble this card but need not obtain acknowledgment of being first.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 defends years of support; revised A5 dictates an acknowledgment of priority and finds a silent way to secure it.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The staircase version expands the audience for spoken praise; this version accepts restrictions on speech and turns credit into a written keepsake.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the cupboard and silence pressure, adding B's earlier wish to scrap it. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 and A5 explicitly seek priority), logic 5 (A3 whispers after B2; A5 writes after B4), relationship 4 (B protects quiet), heightening 4 (A5 creates a lasting record), specificity 4 (A1 establishes shared history), brevityWit 4 (A5's keepsake follows enforced silence): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B remains the cupboard's spokesperson; performance must make that allegiance active rather than merely relaying convenient obstacles.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D154-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ca34e4c9cad6c62c4a9b9d1686a12417317886c4d0f3280ac16c933b55e0aa09\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands a choice, but shrinking people and a growing room could coexist, weakening the required incompatibility.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3's mover and van sizes do not clearly follow the alternatives; A5 abandons moving the sofa for biscuits.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 questions relevance and B4 chooses, but B has no further moving constraint.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's biscuit order changes subjects instead of increasing commitment to the sofa plan.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 naturally gives the pair a shared sofa-moving task.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 is efficient, but A5's ordinary-sized biscuits are a detachable consequence joke.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 55\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before we move the sofa: are we shrinking while the room stays normal, or is the room growing while we stay normal?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Whichever gets this move finished.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Shrinking means call full-sized help. Growing means hurry before the door gets farther away. Choose.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We're shrinking. I'll call my brother.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tell him to bring tweezers. He'll need to collect us afterward.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D154 makes B choose between incompatible accounts so one account determines the group's next actions.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Offering two fanciful possibilities is insufficient unless choosing one commits the group to a different course.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 leaves the explanations jointly possible; revised A1 fixes what stays normal and A3 assigns each exclusive account a different plan.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a turns a moving partner's impatience into a rescue plan; alternative b turns a caterer's timing decision into preparation for gravity's return.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the sofa move and made the alternatives exclusive. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 specifies incompatible accounts), logic 5 (A3 addresses B2's deadline; A5 uses B4's brother), relationship 4 (B wants the move finished), heightening 4 (A5 adds rescuing the movers), specificity 4 (A1 gives the shared task), brevityWit 4 (A5's tweezers follow shrinking): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The explicit exclusions make A1 longer than conversational ideal, though the entire scene remains under 75 words.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D154-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"44c51f8b759965e5ed7e348c5911df9e9d987139750bf7f7f1bd1bab63571138\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers gravity being late or people being early, but those accounts are neither clearly incompatible nor operationally distinct.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 uses B4's choice of late gravity, while A3 never explains how being early would change lunch.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 rejects the premise and B4 selects an answer without revealing a practical concern.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes a landing precaution, but lunch waiting remains only vaguely established in A3.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 does not identify floating objects or a setting; lunch appears only in A3.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's landing sandwiches are concise, but the missing physical setup makes the image harder to play.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 55\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The sandwiches are floating. Is gravity late for lunch, or has it resigned? We need a serving plan.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The guests arrive in five minutes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Late means plates underneath. Resigned means string on every sandwich. Which are we doing?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Late. We haven't enough string.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then fetch the deep plates. We may get the whole buffet at once.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D154 makes a selected impossible explanation govern a concrete collective plan.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D151 recruits belief in one useful explanation; D154 requires a decision between two competing explanations with different consequences.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 ties late gravity to plates and resigned gravity to string, so B4's choice directly determines A5's equipment request.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The sofa version escalates to collecting shrinking people; this version makes B's shortage and guest deadline determine a catering precaution.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the unclear early/late distinction with temporary absence versus resignation, establishing a new buffet setting. Internal reread: fidelity 4 (A1 frames competing work statuses), logic 5 (A3 uses B2's deadline; A5 develops B4's late choice), relationship 4 (B4 supplies a shortage), heightening 4 (A5 anticipates simultaneous landing), specificity 5 (A1 and B2 make service playable), brevityWit 4 (A5 earns the buffet image): 86.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The incompatibility relies on ordinary meanings of being late for an expected duty versus having quit that duty.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D155-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"46e72c894b81ba1b90761e90adf9fc43e2c83dd9948d6be3315eef26e8d86bb7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks for breakfast positioned for a hungry ceiling, although A5 comments on belief rather than requesting a premise-dependent choice.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's hunger objection; A5 directly accepts B4's spoon suggestion.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 offers practical help, but B2 gives little indication of what B personally needs.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 approves the spoon without adapting the action to the ceiling or increasing commitment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies breakfast and a top shelf; A3 supplies a liftable bowl.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'useful kind of belief' states an abstract lesson instead of continuing the concrete scene.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 67\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The ceiling's hungry. Turn the breakfast tray upside down so it can eat.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That's our last porridge.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep half for us. Just turn its bowl over.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll use the tray to catch anything it drops.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. Hold it under the light fitting; that's where it dribbled yesterday.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D155 makes A request a concrete choice whose practical sense depends on the impossible premise being true.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D152 seeks a test of truth; D155 asks for accommodation of the premise without needing proof.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 places food for a ceiling; revised A1 requests inversion for feeding, and A5 treats B's catch-tray offer as normal care.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a bargains over shared food and welcomes help; alternative b accommodates a time-travelling relative by changing how a chair is reserved.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept ceiling breakfast and replaced the abstract closing with a specific feeding arrangement. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 requests upside-down service), logic 5 (A3 preserves B2's porridge; A5 locates B4's tray), relationship 4 (B protects shared breakfast), heightening 4 (A5 adds established care knowledge), specificity 4 (A1 supplies tray and meal), brevityWit 4 (A5's dribbling develops feeding): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 supplies new history about the light fitting; it should read as practical knowledge rather than a separate invented joke.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D155-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b658d0245980c0cd5fb78e84eebe1bab89aa4661894c045c6cbd9f03a5be9311\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 1, \"evidence\": \"A1 reserves a chair before an RSVP, an ordinary precaution that does not require an impossible premise.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's missing reply and A5 answers B4's request for a chair label.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 raises uncertainty and B4 helps with administration, but neither gives the reservation much cost.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's reserved sign repeats the ordinary action in A1 without making time travel operational.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a visitor and chair but does not establish that the visitor comes from another time.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'until time catches up' is concise but decorates a conventional reservation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 50\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your sister's arriving backward through time. Put her chair away so it'll be here when she leaves.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm setting places for dinner.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. Her departure is our arrival. Fold hers first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll label it so nobody unfolds it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Write 'occupied.' That's how we keep it available for her.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D155 asks B to make a specific practical choice that depends on an impossible premise.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Optimistic preparation can reserve an ordinary chair without any impossible belief; this card requires a choice ordinary circumstances would not justify.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1's advance reservation is commonplace; revised A1 asks B to remove a guest's chair precisely to provide it through reversed time.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The ceiling scene negotiates scarce food; this scene relies on family hospitality and reverses the ordinary meaning of making a seat available.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Made the visitor explicitly travel backward through time in a new family-dinner setting. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1's removal depends on reversed time), logic 4 (A3 answers dinner preparation; A5 supplies B4's label), relationship 4 (B wants places ready), heightening 4 (A5 commits to an inverted reservation), specificity 4 (A1 identifies sister and chair), brevityWit 4 (A5's occupied label develops the premise): 86.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The local reversed-time logic requires acceptance on its own terms; it is less immediately intuitive than the ceiling's feeding arrangement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D156-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"090cccfbf4dfa890a3e6e95adc0b524ec2e6dd04f21f5f65653ea12bdb621265\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 allows eve